# @kintsugi/fracture/inport — the OPERATIONAL fracture species that
# names the pattern "a shard body invokes symbols from family-root @X
# but does NOT declare `in @X` in its import block." The absence of
# the `in @X` declaration IS the fracture; inserting the missing `in`
# statement IS the discharge; the sheaf-inclusion invariant IS the
# geometry the fracture defends.
#
# Species under @kintsugi/fracture at sheaf-inclusion altitude.
# Sixteenth landed sibling to the fifteen existing fracture bodies
# (angle_to_paren, bilateral_arm_redundant, cold_compile_within_tolerance,
# dark_count_monotone, docblock_extractive, docblock_incoherent,
# docblock_ungrounded, gate, keyword, operator_match, parent_cycle,
# partials_align, relocate, restart_storm, symbol_lift). Same shape:
# typed carrier + detect action + resolution action + composed
# bilateral discipline.
#
# === Substrate authority (Alex 2026-07-23 verbatim, load-bearing) ===
#
# In-transcript with Reed after Reed's grep-verify of missing
# `in @metalogue` imports across shards:
#
#   > "But like for real. My understanding is that `in` imports a
#      shard, hence a sheaf, hence CREATES the geometric space from
#      which the new shard can be minted."
#
#   > "That needs to be an explicit boundary. Not soft. Otherwise we
#      have implicit sheaf gluing and nobody wants that. That would be
#      geometric JavaScript."
#
# Immediately after Reed enumerated three enforcement-state
# possibilities, Alex named the fracture species by substrate-poetry:
#
#   > "That sounds like a @kintsugi/fracture/inport using a @shard
#      which is not `in`ported"
#
# Ratified substrate-poetry: **inport = `in`-port**. The composition
# portal the `in` keyword declares. A shard using symbols from @X
# without declaring `in @X` violates sheaf-inclusion. That violation
# IS a @kintsugi/fracture/inport.
#
# === The load-bearing geometric invariant ===
#
# `in @X` is a **sheaf-inclusion morphism**. It opens a chart on the
# sheaf @X. The shard being minted lives as a section over the union
# of opened charts. Cross-shard composition requires explicit chart
# overlap declaration. No explicit `in @X`, no valid overlap → no
# valid section → no valid shard.
#
# Not soft. Explicit boundary. Compiler-load-bearing.
#
# Anti-pattern name: **geometric JavaScript** (implicit sheaf gluing;
# prototype-chain-substrate; any shard can implicitly reach any
# other; unauditable). The substrate MUST NOT be that.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/kintsugi/fracture/inport.mirror`.** Clean
#    mint at species-decl altitude. Sixteenth sibling under the
#    @kintsugi/fracture family.
# 2. **`inport`** — Alex 2026-07-23 substrate-poetry naming. The word
#    is `in`-port: the composition portal the `in` keyword declares.
#    Grep confirmed no prior usage in the substrate (shards/**/*.mirror
#    + docs/**/*.md).
# 3. **`import_missing`** rejected — bureaucratic CS-vocab; fails the
#    delightfully-boring audit ("wait, what IS an import in mirror?").
#    Alex's `inport` reads as inevitable to a reader who has grasped
#    the substrate geometry: the `in` keyword is a port; a missing
#    port IS a fracture.
# 4. **`composition_undeclared`** rejected — reads as a philosophical
#    statement rather than a mechanical detector. Not delightfully-
#    boring; not substrate-poetry.
# 5. **`in` as substrate keyword** — landed at `shards/mirror/spec/*`
#    and every `.mirror` file's opening block. The keyword's semantics
#    IS sheaf-chart-opening; this species names the fracture when the
#    keyword is missing.
# 6. **`sheaf-inclusion`** as mathematical vocabulary — Grothendieck
#    sheaves + chart-opening semantics are the canonical mathematical
#    grounding for the invariant; math foundation cites the standard
#    sheaf theory at `docs/math/2026-07-23-kintsugi-fracture-inport-
#    sheaf-inclusion.md`.
# 7. **`geometric JavaScript`** — Alex 2026-07-23 anti-pattern
#    coinage; the failure mode this species DEFENDS AGAINST.
#    Prototype-chain-substrate as CS ancestor; the substrate refuses
#    that shape at species-decl altitude.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (via `in` imports above; each one dogfoods the invariant
# this species enforces):
#   @prism, @meta, @glass                — substrate-decl discipline
#   @nl                                    — `#` comment primitive
#   @kintsugi                              — process-side family-root
#   @kintsugi/fracture                     — family-root; sixteenth
#                                             sibling species under the
#                                             fracture pattern
#   @kintsugi/mend                         — the ACTION that discharges
#                                             the fracture-to-shard
#                                             morphism; the `discharge`
#                                             action below composes
#                                             over `@kintsugi/mend.mend`
#                                             to materialize the
#                                             correction as an inserted
#                                             `in` statement at shard
#                                             top (companion species
#                                             landed 2026-07-23 by Mara)
#   @kintsugi/roomba                       — walker that dispatches
#                                             this species' `detect`
#                                             action per pulse via
#                                             fracture_species discrim-
#                                             inator
#   @fractal                               — vessel family-root
#   @fractal/shard                         — the RETURN SHAPE of the
#                                             tournament-crystallized
#                                             correction (Mara 2026-07-23
#                                             sibling landing; the
#                                             mend's output is a shard
#                                             carrying the inserted
#                                             `in` statement)
#   @fate                                  — tournament dispatch for
#                                             candidate `in @<family>`
#                                             corrections; the
#                                             `propose_correction`
#                                             action rolls the dice over
#                                             the sheaf-inclusion
#                                             candidate space
#   @mirror/store                          — content-addressed fracture
#                                             record store; each
#                                             inport_fracture is
#                                             identified by its
#                                             (shard_position, invoked_
#                                             symbol) content-address
#   @io/fs                                 — file bytes for shard body
#                                             + import-block extraction;
#                                             discharge composes over
#                                             `@io/fs.mutate_at` at
#                                             import-block top offset
#   @epistemologic/pact/bilateral          — bilateral shape below;
#                                             the three predicates
#                                             dogfood the reflective-
#                                             corpus discipline
#
# Consumers (compose over this species, forward-promised at this tick):
#   `mirror kintsugi <shard>` — Reed post-mint CLI empirical
#                                   discharge; dispatches `detect` +
#                                   emits inport_fracture list as
#                                   questions
#   `mirror kintsugi --roomba <shard>` — Reed post-mint CLI empirical
#                                   discharge; dispatches
#                                   `propose_correction` +
#                                   `discharge` in sequence; the
#                                   roomba walks + fills fractures
#                                   until fixed-point
#   @kintsugi/roomba.bump                 — roomba's bump-pulse
#                                   dispatch composes this species'
#                                   detect action via fracture_species
#                                   open enum extension
#
# === Rice-safety ===
#
# The fracture predicate is **grep-decidable**: finite predicate over
# a finite shard-import graph. For each invoked symbol `s` in shard
# `S`:
#
#   1. Extract `family_root(s)` — the `@X` prefix (byte-visible
#      substring operation at @nl altitude).
#   2. Extract `import_block(S)` — the sequence of `in @Y` statements
#      at S's top (byte-visible; deterministic parse).
#   3. Check `family_root(s) ∈ { Y : "in @Y" ∈ import_block(S) }`
#      (finite set membership).
#
# No dynamic dispatch, no aliasing analysis, no program semantics.
# Whole-tick Rice-safe by construction. See `docs/math/2026-07-23-
# kintsugi-fracture-inport-sheaf-inclusion.md` §5 for the mechanical-
# decidability proof.
#
# === The autopoietic discharge pipeline ===
#
# Six-step loop (per Mara #152 autopoietic-loop formalization; Mara
# #159 + #160 forward-promise discharge):
#
#   1. **detect**    — @kintsugi/roomba walks shard bodies; for each
#                       shard, greps invoked symbols vs declared
#                       imports; emits inport_fracture records.
#   2. **propose**   — @fate tournament dispatches candidate
#                       `in @<family_root>` additions per fracture.
#   3. **tournament** — @fate.roll ranks candidates by
#                       @fractal/shard.through-restriction fit.
#   4. **crystallize** — @fractal/shard.materialize crystallizes the
#                       winning candidate as a shard carrying the
#                       inserted `in` statement.
#   5. **mend**      — @kintsugi/mend.mend composes over
#                       @io/fs.mutate_at to insert the `in` statement
#                       at import-block top.
#   6. **verify**    — re-run detect; the specific fracture no
#                       longer fires; fixed-point at that position.
#
# **This IS the empirical proof of autopoietic loop closure.**
# Discharges Reed forward-promise tasks #159 (wire six-step loop
# through apply_h::act) + #160 (empirical one-fracture autopoietic
# round-trip demonstration) against ONE well-defined fracture class.
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] — this species IS a
#   shard-decl; the roomba composition edge reads the shard at parse
#   time via the reflective loader.
# [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]] — verdict is
#   `@glass.verdict`; source_position is `@glass.source_position`;
#   both types inherit through the glass wall.
# [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]] — this species IS the
#   operational half at the sheaf-inclusion altitude.
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] — `prism
#   @kintsugi/fracture/inport` declares the species IS a prism.
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (~74th+ landed instance)
#   — every primitive this species composes over was already landed
#   (@kintsugi/mend + @fractal/shard companion mints today; @fate,
#   @kintsugi/roomba, @io/fs, @epistemologic/pact/bilateral prior);
#   ZERO new machinery beyond the three artifacts (shard-decl +
#   spec + math).
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] — action bodies (detect, propose_
#   correction, discharge) `\`-obligation-blocked at species altitude;
#   discharge at realisation via the reflective evaluator + @io
#   boundary.
# [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]] — this species is a shard-
#   decl + spec + math triad; ZERO new Rust authorship in this arc.
#   Reed post-mint CLI wire dispatches through apply_h::act sentinel-
#   check arms only.
# [[feedback-cli-subcommand-nesting-is-geometric]] — the CLI verb
#   surface `mirror kintsugi` + `mirror kintsugi --roomba` reads
#   the shard-decl composition graph declared here; Alex 2026-07-23
#   named this arc as the "Last Responsible Moment for the CLI
#   design surface and @gestalt rendering shebang."
# [[feedback-legibility-over-foundation-when-collapsing]] — the shape
